## What I implemented
`bowling.py` — `BowlingGame` with:
- `roll(pins)`: appends to flat roll list; validates `0 ≤ pins ≤ 10`, rejects rolling after game completion (`IndexError`), rejects frame sums > 10 (`ValueError`) including the 10th-frame bonus-pairing rule (a 2nd bonus can only be a strike if the 1st bonus was a strike).
- `score()`: raises `IndexError` unless all 10 frames complete (incl. required fill balls); otherwise returns the running total via the 10-frame strike/spare/open walk.
- Helpers `_is_complete()` / `_next_roll_constraint()` implement completeness + next-roll sum constraint from the same frame-walk.

